# This directory holds the on-disk cache for scripts/check-demo-urls.js.
#
# check-demo-urls.js writes ONE JSON file here (demo-url-cache.json) keyed by
# URL -> { status, checkedAt }. The cache lets repeat runs skip re-fetching any
# URL that was checked within the TTL (7 days), so a second run is cheap and
# mostly offline.
#
# This .gitkeep keeps the directory present in a fresh checkout (git does not
# track empty directories) so the script can write the cache file without first
# having to create the directory. The generated cache JSON itself is runtime
# state and is intentionally NOT committed.
